[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
Akvorado requires Kafka and ClickHouse, which are not installed by this
package. They can run on this host or elsewhere.

1. Review the configuration files in %%ETCDIR%%, created from the
   .sample files on the first installation. In particular, check the Kafka
   and ClickHouse addresses in akvorado.yaml, then run:

     akvorado orchestrator %%ETCDIR%%/akvorado.yaml --check

2. The samples are adapted to run every service on a single host, each with
   its own HTTP port:

     orchestrator  :8080  (configuration served to the other services)
     inlet         :8081  (flows on UDP 2055 NetFlow, 4739 IPFIX, 6343 sFlow)
     outlet        :8082  (BMP on TCP 10179)
     console       :8083  (web interface)

   SO_REUSEPORT does not load-balance UDP flows on FreeBSD, so the inlet
   uses one worker per listening port.

3. Enable the services you need in /etc/rc.conf, for example:

     sysrc akvorado_orchestrator_enable=YES akvorado_inlet_enable=YES \
           akvorado_outlet_enable=YES akvorado_console_enable=YES

   Services are supervised by daemon(8) and restarted every 10 seconds
   (akvorado_restart_delay) until Kafka, ClickHouse and the orchestrator are
   reachable. Logs go to syslog, tagged with the service name.

GeoIP databases are looked up in %%LOCALBASE%%/share/GeoIP (see
net/geoipupdate). The full installation guide, including Kafka and
ClickHouse, is at:

  https://github.com/cleberalves40/akvorado/blob/main/console/data/docs/15-freebsd.md
EOM
}
]
